{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.MaximalTorusSu2","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.MaximalTorusSu2","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityLieRank"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2_weight_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2_weight_count","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L120-L121","doc":"V_{1/2} has 2 weight spaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2_torus_rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2_torus_rank","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L116-L118","doc":"T has rank 1 (≅ U(1)) — derived, via `su2MaximalTorus.rank_one`, from\n`su2ComplexifiedRank_eq_one` and ultimately `QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_eq_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2MaximalTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2MaximalTorus","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L102-L114","doc":"The maximal torus data for SU(2).\n\n`rank` is populated by `su2ComplexifiedRank = rank 𝔰𝔩₂(ℂ)` and its `= 1`\nproof by `su2ComplexifiedRank_eq_one` — so the rank-one datum bottoms out at\nthe proved `QOU.Atomicity.sl2_rank_eq_one`, not at `rfl`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:maximal-torus-su2","label":"ex:maximal-torus-su2","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weights_are","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weights_are","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L100-L100","doc":"The weight list for V_{1/2}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weights","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The weights of V are ±1/2 (represented as ±1 in the twice-weight convention). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.rank_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.rank_one","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L96-L96","doc":"T has rank 1 (one-dimensional torus ≅ U(1)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.rank","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Rank of the maximal torus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weight_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.weight_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L92-L92","doc":"V decomposes into 2 weight spaces (±1/2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.numWeightSpaces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.numWeightSpaces","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L90-L90","doc":"Number of weight spaces in the fundamental V = ℂ². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L88-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.SU2MaximalTorusData","kind":"structure","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L84-L100","doc":"**SU(2) maximal torus data**: T ≅ U(1) with 2 weight spaces.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:maximal-torus-su2}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2ComplexifiedRank_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2ComplexifiedRank_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**`rank 𝔰𝔩₂(ℂ) = 1` — DERIVED from the proved `sl2_rank_eq_one`.**\nThis is the atomicity Lie-rank theorem (built from the `ad h` charpoly\n`X³ − 4X`, trailing degree `1`) instantiated at ℂ (an infinite field with\n`2 ≠ 0`). It replaces the former structure-field fiat `rank_one := rfl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.su2ComplexifiedRank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.su2ComplexifiedRank","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L66-L74","doc":"**The SU(2) maximal-torus rank, as the complexified Lie-algebra rank.**\n`= LieAlgebra.rank ℂ (sl (Fin 2) ℂ)`. The `Module.Finite`/`Module.Free`\ninstances (needed to form `LieAlgebra.rank`) come from the 𝔰𝔩₂ triple basis\n`QOU.Atomicity.sl2Basis`; both are Prop-valued, so they agree with the\ninstances used inside `sl2_rank_eq_one` by proof irrelevance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.q_param","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Examples.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Examples.R_q","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus-su2.lean#L43-L45","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}